module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_step_carries_a_script_that_reads_env_the_step_never_binds

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_step_carries_a_script_that_reads_env_the_step_never_binds: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_step_carries_a_script_that_reads_env_the_step_never_binds" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the token-mint prelude declares the environment variables its script reads and a generated step derives its env bindings from that declaration, so a step carrying the prelude cannot omit a binding it reads" } },

  receipts: [
    "**a generated workflow step carries a script that reads an environment variable the step's own env never binds, so the step dies at run time with an unbound-variable error** (INVALID STATE: a RunStep whose run text reads $VAR while its env omits VAR; HARM: the step refuses before doing any work, found only by running the workflow). The script and the env are two facts of one step with no join between them.",

    "WHY IT SURVIVES REVIEW AND TESTING. A witness that checks the script is PRESENT in the emitted step (DESIGN section 3 pairing gap: the supplied side without the route) is green while the script's inputs are unbound; the prelude is spliced in from a shared helper, so the step's author sees neither the read nor the missing binding.",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-10-23 (#14772 -> fleet-converge run 39879022568, srv3). The Runner host files step carried the org-admin token prelude, which reads $WIF_ACCESS_TOKEN, while its env bound only the expected-host and cap-budget names. The step died at prelude line 10; no host argv had issued.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: for every emitted RunStep, derive the variables its run text reads and join them to the names its env binds; a read with no binding is the defect. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- found in production. RUNG NOW: mitigatable. The witness test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_roster_token_prelude_witness every_generated_step_reading_the_wif_token_binds_it exists, with a discriminating RED control and a binding-drop mutation, but no required lane evaluates it (DESIGN Building and checks; gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn), so dropping the binding again would still merge green. Restoration is the native compiler judging that witness population, or enrolling the witness as a row of emitted_subject_build_rows. NEXT TRIGGER: generalize from the one declared name (workload_identity_token_env) to every variable a prelude declares it reads, once AppInstallationTokenMint carries that declaration."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
